(542273, 54028, 10360, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tfaust:</b></div><hr/><i>An excellent shot from an airplace window.  Wow - where was this?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I took this over the Swiss Alps while flying from Zurich to Rome.  The veiw was overwhelming, the phot9o bvarley does it justice.</td>', 'Originally posted by tfaust:An excellent shot from an airplace window.  Wow - where was this?  I took this over the Swiss Alps while flying from Zurich to Rome.  The veiw was overwhelming, the phot9o bvarley does it justice.', '2004-01-14 09:47:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(542278, 54028, 10360, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rooster:</b></div><hr/><i>what a great shot. Too bad about that wing, eh? kinda ruins it.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I kind of like the wing.  I actually took a few without the wing but it just added so much perspective.  Also I liked the contrast of the technological wing against the mountain backdrop.</td>', 'Originally posted by Rooster:what a great shot. Too bad about that wing, eh? kinda ruins it.  I kind of like the wing.  I actually took a few without the wing but it just added so much perspective.  Also I liked the contrast of the technological wing against the mountain backdrop.', '2004-01-14 09:50:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(542307, 53982, 3102, '<td valign="top">A few folks have asked "how was this done?"  My answer is:  "I don''t know!"  I simply shot my footprints in the snow, and this was the result.  Very bizarre!  It was a sunny day with strong shadows, and I guess this all of those elements come together to form a bit of an optical illusion in this case.</td>', 'A few folks have asked "how was this done?"  My answer is:  "I don''t know!"  I simply shot my footprints in the snow, and this was the result.  Very bizarre!  It was a sunny day with strong shadows, and I guess this all of those elements come together to form a bit of an optical illusion in this case.', '2004-01-14 10:05:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(542317, 53459, 12095, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments!  It was a lot of work but the end result was worth it!  Glad you guys &amp; gals liked it!<br/> <br/>There were several suggestions about cropping out the clock at the top and the antenna on the right side of the picture.  Actually it is not a clock.  It is the temperature and compass.  SE stands for southeast. The temperature I did not really care about but the compass I wanted in the picture. The idea was although I do not know where the future will take me I will not fear it because I believe I am headed in the right direction now despite the past.  I am now guided by faith, belief, God, higher power, a moral compass etc which the compass at the top symbolizes.  It was a sub idea but I guess in the end it proved to be  more of a distraction. <br/> <br/>The antenna was an oversight.  Should have removed it before the shoot but luckily I can remove it post challenge via Clone brush. ; )<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments!  It was a lot of work but the end result was worth it!  Glad you guys & gals liked it! There were several suggestions about cropping out the clock at the top and the antenna on the right side of the picture.  Actually it is not a clock.  It is the temperature and compass.  SE stands for southeast. The temperature I did not really care about but the compass I wanted in the picture. The idea was although I do not know where the future will take me I will not fear it because I believe I am headed in the right direction now despite the past.  I am now guided by faith, belief, God, higher power, a moral compass etc which the compass at the top symbolizes.  It was a sub idea but I guess in the end it proved to be  more of a distraction.  The antenna was an oversight.  Should have removed it before the shoot but luckily I can remove it post challenge via Clone brush. ; )', '2004-01-14 10:14:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(542329, 54032, 12095, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture! Congrats on the win!  This was the picture I was worried would beat my second place pic. ;) <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Beautiful picture! Congrats on the win!  This was the picture I was worried would beat my second place pic. ;)    ', '2004-01-14 10:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
