(542625, 53145, 12543, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments!<br/>1st off... im very sorry about the missing "r" :)<br/>Ok the thing is here in iceland everybody buys there own fireworks and sometims spend up to $2000-$4000 on them. I consider theat waste of money like smoking is so thats where the title comes from :)</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments!1st off... im very sorry about the missing "r" :)Ok the thing is here in iceland everybody buys there own fireworks and sometims spend up to $2000-$4000 on them. I consider theat waste of money like smoking is so thats where the title comes from :)', '2004-01-14 12:13:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(542697, 53717, 10799, '<td valign="top">I am just a beginner any comments and critiques are welcome.  I got one comment during the challenge about it being in the middle of the photo.... I did not think it was.  I clearly see more space on the right of the photo than the left.  Should it have been all the way to one side of the picture?  Am I doing better making sure the focus is not too soft?</td>', 'I am just a beginner any comments and critiques are welcome.  I got one comment during the challenge about it being in the middle of the photo.... I did not think it was.  I clearly see more space on the right of the photo than the left.  Should it have been all the way to one side of the picture?  Am I doing better making sure the focus is not too soft?', '2004-01-14 12:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(542739, 53459, 13247, '<td valign="top">i am amazed that is a magnificent pic great job</td>', 'i am amazed that is a magnificent pic great job', '2004-01-14 12:55:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(542745, 53459, 12095, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Konador:</b></div><hr/><i>Congrats on your ribbon :) I was just wondering, why did you use a TV, and not just print the picture and sellotape it to the mirror? That would have been a lot simpler by the sounds of what you went through :P</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I actually thought of that.  The problem with that idea is it was much too dark in the car for the picture to show in the mirror. I would have had to shine a light on to the mirror for it to work. The additional light on the mirror would then spill over to the mirror frame window etc plus it would not look as real as a reflected image in the mirror. The TV on the other hand was a real reflection of light and therefore looked more realistic.</td>', 'Originally posted by Konador:Congrats on your ribbon :) I was just wondering, why did you use a TV, and not just print the picture and sellotape it to the mirror? That would have been a lot simpler by the sounds of what you went through :P  I actually thought of that.  The problem with that idea is it was much too dark in the car for the picture to show in the mirror. I would have had to shine a light on to the mirror for it to work. The additional light on the mirror would then spill over to the mirror frame window etc plus it would not look as real as a reflected image in the mirror. The TV on the other hand was a real reflection of light and therefore looked more realistic.', '2004-01-14 12:57:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(542818, 53114, 47, '<td valign="top">nothing better than computer users that don''t know how to use computers.<br/> <br/>&lt;3</td>', 'nothing better than computer users that don''t know how to use computers. <3', '2004-01-14 13:16:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(542899, 54104, 10546, '<td valign="top">Hello everyone! Thanks for your votes.<br/> <br/>Yes, I also expected the photo to finish better: the commenters had an average of 7.2 but the general voting was 5.4. <br/> <br/>Actualy this was not my first choice, but all other takes turned out worst soo I submited this one. I knew I had a photo on the top 50% before submitting, but after reading the coments, was building a hope to place among all the other "quit smoking"s. Such is life.<br/> <br/>Oh well, off to the next challenge we go...</td>', 'Hello everyone! Thanks for your votes. Yes, I also expected the photo to finish better: the commenters had an average of 7.2 but the general voting was 5.4.  Actualy this was not my first choice, but all other takes turned out worst soo I submited this one. I knew I had a photo on the top 50% before submitting, but after reading the coments, was building a hope to place among all the other "quit smoking"s. Such is life. Oh well, off to the next challenge we go...', '2004-01-14 13:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
