(548852, 53302, 9411, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Well, from the looks of this shot it is obviously something you do need to watch!  You look like your riding a major sucrose high.. very funny.<br/> <br/>But, the shot itself.<br/> <br/>While amusing, it is really one that falls into the category of snapshot.  All the clutter behind you is very distracting, the light is rather harsh on the, um,, cupcakes ?. I like the composition within the frame of the shot that is quite good.<br/> <br/>If you had managed to stick those things over your eyes without the packet and had a plain background this would have been really good.<br/> <br/>of course, this is just my opinion.<br/> <br/>JC  (how''s the resolution doing?)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Well, from the looks of this shot it is obviously something you do need to watch!  You look like your riding a major sucrose high.. very funny. But, the shot itself. While amusing, it is really one that falls into the category of snapshot.  All the clutter behind you is very distracting, the light is rather harsh on the, um,, cupcakes ?. I like the composition within the frame of the shot that is quite good. If you had managed to stick those things over your eyes without the packet and had a plain background this would have been really good. of course, this is just my opinion. JC  (how''s the resolution doing?)', '2004-01-19 12:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(548858, 54006, 9411, '<td valign="top">Greatings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>I think this is a very well done image. I like the concept, use of Black and White, the mirror.<br/> <br/>The composition could use a little tweaking. Possibly a little less negative space, right foreground. THe DOF is right on.<br/> <br/>Well done in my opinion.<br/>JC</td>', 'Greatings from the Critique Club. I think this is a very well done image. I like the concept, use of Black and White, the mirror. The composition could use a little tweaking. Possibly a little less negative space, right foreground. THe DOF is right on. Well done in my opinion.JC', '2004-01-19 12:12:15.000000', NULL, 0),
